.TH MATHWAVE 1 "November 2026" "mathwave 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mathwave \- terminal audio visualizer that drives a grid of math functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mathwave
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mathwave
captures the audio your system is playing, the same way
.BR cava (1)
does, and turns it into a grid of panels. Each panel plots one math
function, and the music moves that function's parameters. The formula is
printed under every plot together with its live parameter values.
.PP
The default panels are: 808 (exponential decay), dive bomb (1/x), Reese
(sum-to-product trig identity), screech (tan x), FM wobble, Fourier-series
saw, sinc, the logistic map, and a classic DFT spectrum.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIMETHOD\fR
auto, pulse, pipewire, fifo, stdin or demo. auto tries
.BR parec (1)
first, then
.BR pw-record (1).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-source " " \fINAME\fR
PulseAudio source or PipeWire target. Default: monitor of the default output.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Play the built-in demo track, in which every sound is generated from a formula.
.TP
.B \-\-audible
With \-\-demo, also send the track to your speakers.
.TP
.BI \-\-panels " LIST"
Comma-separated panel keys, for example 808,reese,tan,spectrum. The group names math and
cern stand for every built-in math panel and the eleven CERN panels. Replaces the pages
setting with this list plus the other group.
.TP
.BI \-\-page " N"
Start on page N. Page 2 is the CERN page by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-layout " auto|COLSxROWS"
Grid layout.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
phonk, ocean, ember, matrix, mono, wal, or chroma (colors follow the note being played).
.TP
.BI \-\-fps " N"
Frames per second (default 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-sensitivity " X"
Gain applied after normalization.
.TP
.BI \-\-fft\-size " N"
FFT size: 1024, 2048 (default), 4096, 8192 or 16384. Larger sizes separate sub-bass from bass better but react a little later.
.TP
.BI \-\-bpm " auto|N"
Detect the tempo from kicks, or fix it at N beats per minute.
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " NAME"
Activate a config profile: sections named like [tune.808@NAME] are merged over the plain ones.
.TP
.BI \-\-focus " N"
Start with panel N full screen.
.TP
.B \-\-meters
Start in the live meter view.
.TP
.B \-\-controls
Start in the full-screen controls view.
.TP
.B \-\-tune
Start in tune mode on the \-\-focus panel (or panel 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-set " NAME=VALUE"
Set a [slider.NAME] at startup. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Do not capture the mouse.
.TP
.B \-\-formulas
Print every panel's formula, drive signal, tuning and sound, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-list\-knobs " [PANEL]"
List the keys a [tune.PANEL] section accepts, with defaults, for every panel or one.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-features
List every band (built-in, [bands] and inline) and feature a drive can use, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-keys
List the keyboard controls and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-render\-wav " PATH"
Write the demo track to a stereo WAV file and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-dump " FRAMES"
Headless mode: simulate the demo and print the last frame (see \-\-size, \-\-at).
.TP
.BI \-p ", " \-\-config " FILE"
Config file. Default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mathwave/config.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B 1\-9, 0
Show that panel full screen with its formula, sound and drive (0 is panel 10). Press the same key again or g to return to the grid.
.TP
.B n, N
Next or previous page. By default page 1 is the panels line and page 2 is the CERN page.
.TP
.B ". ,"
Focus the next or previous panel, which reaches panel 11 and beyond.
.TP
.B k
Tune mode: the focused panel's drive, level shaping, smoothing and formula knobs as
sliders beside it. From the grid it opens panel 1.
.TP
.B c
Full-screen controls: every [slider.NAME], with which panels read it.
.TP
.B Up, Down, Tab
Pick a slider in tune mode, the controls view, or a controls panel in the grid.
.TP
.B Left, Right
Move it. Shift+Left/Right or [ and ] move ten steps; Home and End jump to the ends.
The mouse can click or drag a slider bar, and the wheel moves the one under it.
.TP
.B d, u, w
Selected slider back to its default; undo all tuning since the last write; write the
tuning into [tune.PANEL] (or [tune.PANEL@PROFILE]) in the config file.
.TP
.B m
Toggle the meter view: every band and feature as a live bar with its value, dB, Hz or note name.
.TP
.B P
Cycle config profiles (Shift+P).
.TP
.B b
Tap tempo. Tap at least twice on the beat. B returns to the configured or detected tempo.
.TP
.B f
Cycle formula detail: full, formula plus values, hidden.
.TP
.B r
Reload the config file. Everything changes at once, including bands and analysis settings,
except the audio input itself (method, source, rate, channels, fifo), which applies on restart.
A config error is shown in the status bar and the running settings are kept.
.TP
.B t
Next color theme.
.TP
.B + \-
Raise or lower gain.
.TP
.B p, space
Pause.
.TP
.B Esc
Close tune mode, the controls view or the meters; from the grid, quit.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH TUNING
Each panel can have a
.B [tune.PANEL]
section in the config file. Keys every panel accepts:
.TP
.B drive
What the panel listens to: a band, a feature (see FEATURES), band(LO, HI) or peak(LO, HI)
inline, or an expression such as max(sub, 0.7*bass).
.TP
.B gain, threshold, curve, min, max
Shape the level, in that order: multiply, ignore everything below the threshold,
raise to the curve exponent, then map into min..max.
.TP
.B attack, decay
Smoothing for this panel only. When set, the panel reads unsmoothed levels, so it can
move faster or slower than the global [smoothing] values.
.TP
.B attack_ms, decay_ms, hold_ms
The same in milliseconds (time to cover 90% of a change), independent of the frame rate,
plus a peak hold.
.PP
Panels also have knobs for their own constants, for example tau and reveal on the 808
panel. Run
.B mathwave \-\-list\-knobs
to see them. A knob can be a number or an expression of drives, for example
.BR "a = 8 + 16*pitch" .
Custom panels can use
.B level
in their params to pick up their tuning.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B [slider.NAME]
range = LO-HI (default 0-10), default (default LO), step (default a hundredth of the
range) and label. NAME becomes a value any drive, knob, shaping key or custom panel
param can read; divide to scale it, for example drive = punch/10. Add
.B controls
to panels to show the sliders in the grid.
.TP
.B Expressions
gain, threshold, curve, min, max and every knob accept expressions of drives and
sliders, for example gain = 0.5 + punch/5.
.TP
.B knobs
In a [panel.NAME] section, knobs = NAME = DEFAULT (LO..HI), ... declares knobs the
panel's params can use, [tune.NAME] can set and tune mode shows.
.TP
.B mouse
on or off under [general] (default on).
.SH CERN PAGE
Eleven panels that follow a proton through the LHC, each plotting the physics of one stage
with real accelerator numbers:
.B rf
(\(*DE = qV\d0\u cos \(*f, steps on the kick),
.B bend
(r = p/(qB) on the 25 m PS Booster ring, magnets from the spectrum),
.B bunch
(bunch splitting, 1 to 32 Gaussians),
.B gamma
(v = c\(sr(1 \- 1/\(*g\u2\d) and how far below c the proton is),
.B cold
(R = 0 below T_c; noisy passages quench the 1.9 K magnets),
.B ramp
(E = \(*gmc\u2\d from 450 GeV to 6.8 TeV, then a beam dump),
.B beams
(two rings from the left and right channels, E_cm = 2E = 13.6 TeV),
.B squeeze
(\(*s* = \(sr(\(*e\(*b*), the hourglass at the collision point),
.B overlap
(L \(pt e^(\-d\u2\d/4\(*s\u2\d)),
.B collide
(a new event with curling tracks on every kick or snare) and
.B higgs
(a diphoton mass histogram whose 125 GeV bump grows with its significance).
Every one has knobs, listed by \-\-list\-knobs, and works in tune mode.
.PP
In [general],
.B pages = math | cern
sets the pages n flips through; separate pages with | and panels with commas.
.SH FREQUENCIES
.TP
.B [bands]
NAME = LO-HI followed by optional words: peak (loudest bin instead of the mean),
range=DB, floor=DB, fall=DB_PER_S, fft=N and norm=own|shared. A new name becomes a drive;
a built-in name (sub, bass, lowmid, mid, highmid, presence, air) is redefined.
.TP
.B [analysis]
fft_size; multires = on with low_fft, high_fft and split_hz; tilt in dB per octave
around 1 kHz; weighting = none|a; pitch_range = LO-HI.
.TP
.B [onsets]
kick, snare and hat take ranges joined with +, such as 180-400 + 2000-5000, plus
sensitivity, refractory_ms and envelope_ms.
.TP
.B [tempo]
bpm = auto|N, multiplier (2 double time, 0.5 half time) and range = LO-HI, the window
detected tempos fold into.
.SH FEATURES
rms, centroid, rolloff, flatness, flux, pitch, note, tonality, kick, snare, hat, phase,
left, right, side, width and balance, all 0..1. Run
.B mathwave \-\-list\-features
for descriptions.
.SH PROFILES
Any section name can end in @NAME. Its keys apply only while profile NAME is active
(\-\-profile, profile under [general], or Shift+P) and are merged over the plain section.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mathwave/config
User configuration. An annotated example is installed at
.IR /usr/share/doc/mathwave/config.example .
Writing from tune mode keeps the previous file as
.IR config.bak .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mathwave/sliders.json
Slider positions, per profile ($XDG_STATE_HOME is honored).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mathwave
mathwave \-\-demo \-\-audible
mathwave \-\-panels 808,dive,reese,tan \-\-layout 2x2
mathwave \-\-meters \-\-profile phonk
mathwave \-\-bpm 140 \-\-theme chroma
mathwave \-i fifo \-\-fifo /tmp/mpd.fifo
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cava (1),
.BR parec (1),
.BR pw-record (1)
